---
layout: default
title: Downloads
permalink: /downloads/
---
// Inspired by: https://syncthing.net/downloads/

article.container
  header
    h1 Downloads

  h3.mt-4.mb-2 ActivityWatch {{ site.data.downloads.stable.version }}

  div.row.mt-4
    | {% for platform in site.data.downloads.stable.platforms %}
    div.col-md-6(id="{{ platform.name }}")
      b {{ platform.name }}
      | {% if platform.name == 'Linux' %}
      p.small.mb-2
        | Choose #[b .zip] to extract and run manually, #[b .AppImage] for a standalone app (mark it executable first), or #[b .deb] for Debian/Ubuntu's package installer. AUR and nixpkgs are distribution packages and may update separately.
      p.small.mb-2
        | Match the download to your CPU: run #[code uname -m] in a terminal. #[code x86_64] means 64-bit Intel/AMD; #[code aarch64] or #[code arm64] means ARM64. Use a matching build only if listed.
      | {% elsif platform.name == 'macOS' %}
      p.small.mb-2
        | Open #[b Apple menu → About This Mac]. A #[b Chip] entry naming Apple M-series means Apple Silicon; an Intel #[b Processor] means Intel. Choose the matching download below.
      | {% endif %}
      ul
        | {% for asset in platform.assets %}
        li
          a(href="{{asset.url}}" style="{% if forloop.first %} font-weight: bold {% endif %}") {{ asset.title }}
          | {{ asset.description }}
        | {% endfor %}
    | {% endfor %}

  p.small.dim.mt-3
    | ActivityWatch is free and community-funded. If it's useful to you, consider #[a(href="/go/?src=download") supporting the project] — it keeps development going and the tool independent.

  | {% if site.data.downloads.prerelease %}
  h3.mt-5.mb-2 Pre-release: ActivityWatch {{ site.data.downloads.prerelease.version }}
  p.small.dim
    | A newer pre-release is available for testing new features and fixes. It may be unstable — for everyday use, prefer the stable release above.
  div.row.mt-2
    | {% for platform in site.data.downloads.prerelease.platforms %}
    div.col-md-6(id="prerelease-{{ platform.name }}")
      b {{ platform.name }}
      ul
        | {% for asset in platform.assets %}
        li
          a(href="{{asset.url}}" style="{% if forloop.first %} font-weight: bold {% endif %}") {{ asset.title }}
          | {{ asset.description }}
        | {% endfor %}
    | {% endfor %}
  | {% endif %}

  div For help on how to get started, see the #[a(href="https://docs.activitywatch.net/en/latest/getting-started.html") Getting Started guide] in the documentation.

  div Looking for an older or pre-release version? You can find all #[a(href="https://github.com/ActivityWatch/activitywatch/releases") releases on GitHub].

  h3.mt-3 Nightly builds
  p
    | Unstable "nightly" builds are automated by our CI setup. These contain yet-unreleased features and bug fixes. See #[a(href="https://github.com/ActivityWatch/activitywatch/issues/507") issue #507] for where to get them.

  h3.mt-4 Watchers

  p #[b What is a watcher?] A watcher is a program or plugin that watches for activity of different kinds and reports it to ActivityWatch.

  p
    | ActivityWatch comes with two watchers preinstalled:
    ul
      li Window watcher: tracks the active application/window
      li AFK watcher: tracks if you're using your mouse and keyboard to determine if you are AFK.
    | #[a(href="https://docs.activitywatch.net/en/latest/watchers.html") The documentation] contains a list of all available watchers (editor plugins, for example).

  h5.mt-3 Web browser watchers
  p Use these web extensions to get more detailed tracking about the websites you visit (such as the URL, or if a tab is playing sound).

  div
    a(href="https://addons.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/addon/aw-watcher-web/").mr-2
      img(src="/img/AMO-get-the-addon-178x60px.png")

    a(href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/activitywatch-web-watcher/nglaklhklhcoonedhgnpgddginnjdadi")
      img(src="/img/ChromeWebStore_BadgeWBorder_v2_206x58.png", height="58")
